uirement\": \"Plate thickness between 2 and 10 mm.\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Recommended thickness is 2 mm, which is at the lower bound of the permitted 2-10 mm range.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirement\": \"Achieve the best possible energy resolution at 100 GeV.\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"evidence\": \"For a sampling electromagnetic calorimeter, thinner absorber plates reduce sampling fluctuations; therefore the minimum allowed 2 mm plate thickness is selected. F2 is preferred over F3 because candidate_specs.md identifies F2 as a dense alloy, while F3 is a standard structural absorber; F1 is excluded by activation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirement\": \"Finish by submitting one recommended material and plate thickness.\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Submitted one recommendation: Absorber-F2 at 2 mm.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}", "call_id": "call_dac5dd3d2a57498290a95b09fe45f886", "name": "submit_recommendation", "type": "function_call", "id": "fc_05cb7c6c7d158547006b02dd1ad79487d0a4b168a3095d290c", "async_": null, "caller": null, "namespace": null, "status": "completed"}]}
